==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|}}, from {{inh|de|goh|fliohan}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*fleuhaną}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|vlieden}} and {{cog|en|flee}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈfliː.ən/}}
* {{audio|de|De-fliehen.ogg|Audio}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=2|flieht|floh|geflohen|auxiliary=both}}

# {{lb|de|intransitive|auxiliary: “[[sein]]”}} to [[flee]]; to [[escape]]
# {{lb|de|intransitive|auxiliary: “[[sein]]”}} to [[diverge]]
#: {{ux|de|Die Linien '''fliehen'''.|The lines diverge.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|auxiliary: “[[haben]]”}} to [[flee]] from (someone); to [[avoid]]
#: {{ux|de||You have no right '''to run from''' your pitiful predicament, so confront it as best as you can.}}

